# Pull requests

`origin` is `lampac-nextgen/TorrServer`. GitHub still treats that repo as a fork of `YouROK/TorrServer`, so `gh pr create` with no `--repo` opens the PR on YouROK.

- Push the branch to `origin` (`git@github.com:lampac-nextgen/TorrServer`).
- Create and update PRs with `--repo lampac-nextgen/TorrServer`. Base is `master` unless the user names another branch.
- Do not open, push to, or comment on `YouROK/TorrServer` unless the user explicitly asks to send the change upstream.

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --repo lampac-nextgen/TorrServer --base master --head "$(git branch --show-current)" --title "..." --body "..."
```

## Merging

Merge with squash, always: `gh pr merge <n> --repo lampac-nextgen/TorrServer --squash`. `master` history is one commit per PR, titled like the PR with the number suffix (`docs: ... (#95)`). Do not use `--merge` or `--rebase`.

- Only merge when the user asks. Never merge on your own, and never enable auto-merge unless asked.
- Put the PR title in conventional-commit form (`fix:`, `test:`, `docs:` ...), since it becomes the commit subject.
- Several small commits on the branch (failing test first, then the fix) are fine: they are squashed away. Keep the explanation in the PR body.
- Before merging, read `gh pr checks`. Name any failing check to the user, and say whether it touches the PR's files.
